    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "SITUATION AND AMENITIES: The property is set well back from the road, overlooking its own grounds. This spacious property is in a prime residential area close to the Golf Club and Lough Corrib, which is just a mile away, with public slip and extensive moorings. Oughterard, which is a mile distant, is well known for its range of shops, pubs, banks and hotels which cater for the large numbers of visitors who come to take advantage of the walking, boating and other leisure activities for which this area is justly famous. Golf is on the doorstep of the property at the 18 hole Oughterard golf course, set in natural parkland and there are six other golf courses within an hour`s drive.\n\nTHE HOUSE: The property is approached by a chipped driveway, leading over a cattle grid, which provides access to the front and side of the property and garage. The property is comfortably set centrally within the site and with semi-maintained gardens to the front and rear. There are areas of the rear garden which backs onto Oughterard golf club that could be cleared and made into formal gardens, if required. The property including the constructed sunroom (circa 32 sq. m.) extends to 210 sq. meters and retention planning permission was granted in 2013, under application number 13/1008. \n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Wooden front door leading into inner hallway.\n\nInner Hallway - 16'10\" (5.13m) x 7'8\" (2.34m)\n(N) being L-shaped in design, with veneered wood flooring throughout, doors leading into sitting room, study, kitchen, utility room and 3-bedrooms, with spiral staircase rising to first floor.\n\nSitting Room - 16'10\" (5.13m) x 15'1\" (4.6m)\n(N, E) with continuation of wood flooring throughout, exposed wooden beams, a beautiful full height cut granite stone open fireplace, television point and stairs rising to dining room.\n\nDining Room - 15'3\" (4.65m) x 9'10\" (3m)\n(S, E) with solid wood flooring throughout, exposed feature wooden beams, wooden double doors leading into proposed conservatory area / sunroom and door leading to kitchen.\n\nKitchen - 15'1\" (4.6m) x 13'1\" (3.99m)\n(S) with large porcelain tiled flooring throughout, a beautifully fitted range of wall mounted and base units, with granite worktops, space for electric oven with extractor above, built-in dishwasher, built-in wine rack, one and a half bowl stainless steel sink drainer and door leading to rear hall.\n\nRear Hall - 6'0\" (1.83m) x 3'6\" (1.07m)\n(S) with continuation of porcelain flooring throughout, space for large fridge freezer, wooden door giving access to rear garden.\n\nUtility Area - 9'3\" (2.82m) x 6'6\" (1.98m)\nwith porcelain tiled flooring throughout, access to hot press and storage cupboard (hot press houses a factory lagged tank), space and plumbing for washing machine and dryer, door leading to shower room.\n\nShower Room - 9'2\" (2.79m) x 5'10\" (1.78m)\n(S) with continuation of porcelain tiled flooring throughout, large walk-in shower cubicle with glass panel, mains pressure wall mounted Drench shower, low level WC, heated towel rail, sink set on mahogany base with storage below, obscured window to rear.\n\nOffice / Bedroom 5 - 9'0\" (2.74m) x 10'5\" (3.18m)\n(N) with wood flooring throughout, views to front.\n\nBedroom 1 - 14'8\" (4.47m) x 9'9\" (2.97m)\n(S) with continuation of solid wood flooring throughout, television point.\n\nBedroom 2 - 12'5\" (3.78m) Max x 9'2\" (2.79m)\n(N) with continuation of solid wood flooring throughout, television point, views to front.\n\nBedroom 3 - 10'2\" (3.1m) x 9'9\" (2.97m)\n(N) with solid wood flooring throughout, television point, views to front.\n\n\nFrom hallway spiral staircase rising to first floor (there is sufficient space to install a standard set of stairs).\n\nLanding - 12'5\" (3.78m) Max x 15'2\" (4.62m) Max\n(S) with carpeted flooring throughout, full range of built-in wardrobes and storage, door to bathroom, bedroom and access to loft, Velux window to rear.\n\nBedroom 4 - 21'5\" (6.53m) x 12'7\" (3.84m)\n(S) with carpeted flooring throughout, two Velux windows to rear, full range of storage.\n\nBathroom - 9'0\" (2.74m) x 5'6\" (1.68m)\n(S) with carpeted flooring throughout, bath with panelled surround, fully tiled walls, low level WC, wash hand basin, wall mounted mirror with light and Velux window to rear.\n\nProposed conservatory / sunroom - 18'0\" (5.49m) x 13'5\" (4.09m)\n(E, S, W) of block construction, insulation, first fix wiring done.\n\nGarage - 27'3\" (8.31m) x 13'6\" (4.11m)\n(N, E, S) is of block construction with a rendered exterior, under a slated roof, manual up and over roller door and also houses the boiler, power.\n\nOutside\nThe property has gardens to the front and rear, interspersed with lovely mature trees and areas of maintained gardens. There is a south facing patio area to the rear overlooking the garden. There is an area of garden left to nature but this could be cleared to provide more formal gardens.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
